  "Node tree: trolley_01 (chassis) root -> wheelEngine_0N -> wheel_0N; clamps, locks and stopperJoint brackets under trolley_01; stopper_0N arms under their stopperJoint_0N bracket (USD joint chain). trashbox_01 (crate) is a separate top-level node (loose body in USD, rests on the deck held by the clamps).",
  "28 revolute joints + 1 fixed (lens, merged into trolley_01).",
  "Steering: each wheelEngine turns about a vertical axis 68 mm inboard of its wheel's centre, so steering also swings the wheel around the kingpin (that is how the USD is rigged); 90 deg is clear of the body (sweep4).",
  "Limits were measured one joint at a time (sweep4). Combining extreme poses (e.g. a stopper arm at +142 deg with its wheel steered 90 deg) can interpenetrate.",
  "No TANGENT attributes on purpose: three.js builds the tangent frame per pixel from UV derivatives, which is the frame the diamond-plate normal map was baked against. The Khronos validator reports 28 MESH_PRIMITIVE_GENERATED_TANGENT_SPACE warnings for this; 0 errors.",
  "Masses are the per-part USD (base.usda) masses; the crate's 39.8 kg includes its liner."
